      "value": "@{5c021357a58d0a7e70c3e515|full_name}: The issue is more that Very Poors have a HUGE range on optimization. As an example, some may have over 800k tris and 30+ lights, while others may be a Poor with only 2 extra material slots which makes it a Very Poor. Providing an \"Insanely Poor\" option or something would be very useful in this situation, since it would help differentiate between \"reasonable\" Very Poor models and everything else",
